					 Accounting Department 
				 
				 The Accounting Department conducts all financial transactions related to cash collections, cash disbursements, employee benefits, and employee payroll in accordance with generally accepted accounting principles. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Adult Activity Center 
				 
				 The Lunenburg Adult Activity Center is a source of service and a place of opportunity - a focal point in the community. We function as an information and referral service for elders and their families. If you have a concern we have staff available to assist you, just give us a call. Open to all people age 50+, in Lunenburg and surrounding communities. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Animal Control Department 
				 
				 Animal Services maintains a safe and secure city by providing a healthy environment for human and animal residents living in our community. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Assessor's Department 
				 
				 The Assessors' primary responsibility is to value all real estate and personal property subject to taxation. Assessed valuations are based on "full and fair cash value" of as of the January 1st preceding each fiscal year.  
				
			 			 
				 
					 Building Department 
				 
				 The Building Department is responsible for ensuring that building and zoning codes are followed to ensure the public welfare. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Electrical Inspector 
				 
				 Electrical Inspector Performs a variety of routine and complex technical duties in the inspection of buildings. Get more details about the Electrical Inspector on this page. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Facilities, Grounds, & Recreation Department 
				 

The Facilities, Grounds, and Recreation Department oversees, supervises, and facilitates the comprehensive management of all town facilities and grounds. It assists the town to strategize, prioritize and coordinate maintenance, repairs, safety, and efficiencies of municipal properties, as well as plays a key role in the future use and reuse of properties. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Fire Department 
				 
				 The Fire Department works to save lives and protect property through prevention, preparedness, education, and response. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Human Resources Department 
				 
				 The Department of Human Resources provides programs and services in support of a high-performing workforce and organizational excellence. Human Resources services include recruitment and employment, compensation and benefits, and wellness programs. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Information Technology Department 
				 
				 Information Technology provides information technology services to various departments, which support the local strategic goals, sub-goals, and objectives. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Land Use Department 
				 
				 Under the general direction of the Town Manager, coordinates the activities of all of the Boards and Departments involved in regulating land use, Get more details about the Land Use Department on this page. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Lunenburg Public Library 
				 
				 Search the card catalog, renew your items, or join us for an event at the library. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Plumbing & Gas Inspector 
				 
				 The Plumbing and Gas Inspector performs a variety of routine and complex technical duties in the inspection of buildings, get more details about the Plumbing / Gas Inspector on this page. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Police Department 
				 
				 The Police Department and its officers work hard to serve and protect the community. Here you can find helpful information about their initiatives, divisions, and more. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Public Works: Sewer, Highway, & Cemetery Department 
				 
				 The Public Works Department is dedicated to planning, developing, and maintaining the County's infrastructure, solid waste program, facilities, and other services in a manner that provides safe travel for the general public and enhances the quality of life. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Town Clerk 
				 
				 The Clerk's Office handles administrative duties such as record keeping, staffing, service counters, screening solicitors, and more. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Town Manager 
				 
				 Lunenburg’s Town Manager is the Chief Administrative and Financial Officer for the town. Get more details about the Town Manager on this page. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Treasurer/Tax Collector Department 
				 
				 The Treasury Department manages funds throughout the municipality. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Veteran's Services Department  
				 
				 The Veteran's Services Department is responsible for providing services to prior service members along with their families. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Weight & Measures Department 
				 
				 Municipal Sealers of Weights and Measures (Sealers) test, seal and inspect commercial weighing and measuring devices located in the municipality where they are locally appointed; after passing written and practical examinations administered by the Division, these individuals inspect retail businesses operating in their municipality for compliance with the unit pricing, item pricing, or price advertising requirements; and investigate consumer complaints about businesses operating in their municipality. 
				
			 						 
					 
		 
	 










	   

	   

			   


		 

	 

	
	 

	 
 
 	 
				                



	 
 
 
 	 
				                



	 
 





	 
	 
		 
